## 3. The big picture: one request, end to end

If the team remembers one diagram from this week, make it this one. It answers the Month 1 checkpoint question.

```text
 CLIENT   POST /v1/loans  {"member_id": ..., "copy_barcode": ...}
   │
   ▼
 UVICORN         the server: listens on a port, hands the request to FastAPI     (M6)
   │
   ▼
 ROUTER          matches method + path; Pydantic validates the body              (M6, M7)
   │             bad shape?  ──► 422, before our code even runs
   ▼
 SERVICE         applies the business rules (exists? available? limit? fines?)   (M1)
   │             rule broken? ──► domain error ──► router maps it to 404 / 409
   │             owns COMMIT / ROLLBACK for the whole operation
   ▼
 REPOSITORY      SQLAlchemy 2.0 builds SQL from a Session                        (M8)
   │
   ▼
 psycopg 3 ──► POSTGRESQL      constraints from Week 3 are the final gate
   │
   ▼
 back up the chain ──► 201 Created + Location header + JSON body

 Around all of it:
   • settings (DATABASE_URL, DEBUG…) come from env vars via pydantic-settings    (M4)
   • API + Postgres run together in Docker Compose with health checks           (M3)
   • pytest drives this whole path through TestClient against a test DB         (M2)
   • GitHub Actions runs ruff + mypy + pytest on every PR, and red blocks merge (M5)
```

