## 10. Quick-fire check for the team

<details>
<summary><b>Click to reveal the answers</b> (try answering first)</summary>

| Question | Answer |
|---|---|
| What's the difference between FastAPI and Uvicorn? | FastAPI is the framework that defines behaviour. Uvicorn is the HTTP server that runs it. |
| Why is search a query parameter but ISBN a path parameter? | The path picks one resource. The query sets options on a collection. |
| Where does "a member may hold at most N loans" belong? | In the **service**. It's a business rule, not HTTP and not data access. |
| Why shouldn't the repository call `commit()`? | Only the service knows if the *whole* operation succeeded. Early commits leave half-finished data. |
| What's the difference between `flush()` and `commit()`? | `flush()` sends the SQL inside the transaction (you get IDs), but it can still be rolled back. `commit()` makes it permanent. |
| Who returns the 422, you or FastAPI? | FastAPI/Pydantic, before your function runs. |
| Why does `localhost:5432` fail inside the API container? | `localhost` is the API container itself. Use the service name `db`. |
| What does `depends_on: condition: service_healthy` add? | The API waits until Postgres passes its health check, not just until the container starts. |
| Does adding `.env` to `.gitignore` fix a secret that was already pushed? | No. Revoke or rotate it. `.gitignore` only stops future tracking. |
| Why does a failing test block a merge? | CI runs on the PR, and branch protection makes the check a required status. |

</details>

